---
functor: 1
title: bend
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`bend` · deform · bend the long axis into an arc, such as a curved arrow; the strokes keep their width.

# Form

`x.bend` on a symbol, `(a + b).bend` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `to.wide.bend` | $to.wide.bend$ | built and cached |
| `to.wide.bend.flipv` | $to.wide.bend.flipv$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Bend the long axis into an arc, such as a curved arrow; the strokes keep their width. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A changed outline of the base. The compiler moves each point of the outline, and the strokes keep their shape and width. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- Bends the long axis into an arc of 60 degrees, with the middle up. Add `flipv` after it to bend down. In a `diagram`, it makes a curved arrow.

# From LaTeX

tikz-cd `bend left` and `bend right` in a `diagram`.

